Package: DropoutKiller
Type: Package
Title: Selective Dropout Recovery for Single-Cell and Multiome Data
Version: 0.8.0
Authors@R: person("DropoutKiller", "Developers", email = "dropoutkiller@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: DropoutKiller Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: DropoutKiller Developers <dropoutkiller@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: Detects and selectively recovers technical zero events in single-cell
    RNA-seq and paired RNA plus ATAC multiome data. The RNA production detector
    applies native-ALRA-style randomized low-rank reconstruction and a gene-wise
    empirical low-rank zero gate within major cell classes, while SuperCell
    memberships and retained hierarchy remain reserved for biologically local
    recovery. For 10x Multiome data, weighted-nearest-neighbor graphs can define
    one frozen multimodal membership shared by RNA and ATAC. ATAC zeros are modeled
    with separate latent accessibility and cell-specific capture states, and
    high-confidence accessible-but-missed coordinates are recovered with
    posterior-accessibility-weighted, capture-aware local Gamma-Poisson empirical
    Bayes estimation. Observed non-dropout values and raw fragment evidence are
    never overwritten.
